71. 车五平七 马９进８ { [%emt 0:02:13] [%think 11758] [%out 12074] [%in 2]
[%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 3443] Two points decide this move. 1. **The
elephant on c9 is not hanging.** The red rook on c6 attacks it, but the e7
elephant covers c9 (the d8 eye is empty). If Rxc9, then e7xc9 wins the rook. If
I moved c9 to a7 instead, e7 would be left unprotected, so neither elephant
should move. 2. **Move the horse from i9 to h7 to hem in the red horse.** From
h7 it blocks the leg the red horse on h6 needs to reach g8 or i8. The red
horse's only useful jump is then f7, which my king covers. My horse on h7 also
covers f8 and f6. If red pushes the pawn i6 to i7 to chase it, the horse can go
back to i9 or g9. If red checks with Rc8, my king goes to f9, where it is still
reasonably safe. My position is behind on material, so I'll keep defending
solidly and play out the move limit. } 72. 兵一进一 马８退７ { [%emt 0:00:59]
